---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj34.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope and Effective Date" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Redefining a Lease — Alignment With IFRS 16" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Single On-Balance-Sheet Lessee Model" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Initial Measurement of the Right-of-Use Asset and Lease Liability" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Subsequent Measurement" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Exemptions — Short-Term and Low-Value Leases" },
        { id: "s8", label: "J-GAAP-Specific Simplifications" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Initial Recognition of a Lease" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example — Applying the Short-Term Lease Exemption" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
  <div class="callout info callout--centered">EFFECTIVE DATE: This Statement was issued September 13, 2024 and takes effect for fiscal years beginning on or after April 1, 2027 — meaning as of the current date, companies are in the preparation/transition period ahead of mandatory adoption. It supersedes the old dual-classification model under ASBJ Statement No. 13 (see the companion poster).</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a>
      <a href="#s2">2. Scope and Effective Date</a>
      <a href="#s3">3. Redefining a Lease — Alignment With IFRS 16</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. The Single On-Balance-Sheet Lessee Model</a>
      <a href="#s5">5. Initial Measurement of the Right-of-Use Asset and Lease Liability</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Subsequent Measurement</a>
      <a href="#s7">7. Exemptions — Short-Term and Low-Value Leases</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. J-GAAP-Specific Simplifications</a>
      <a href="#s9">9. Worked Example — Initial Recognition of a Lease</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Worked Example — Applying the Short-Term Lease Exemption</a>
      <a href="#s11">11. Disclosure Requirements</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</a>
      <a href="#s13">13. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a>
      <a href="#s14">14. Statement Mapping</a>
      <a href="#s15">15. Related Standards</a>
      <a href="#s16">16. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Bringing substantially all leases onto the lessee's Balance Sheet</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 34 ELIMINATES the OLD dual finance/operating lessee classification model (previously governed by ASBJ Statement No. 13 — see the companion poster) and requires recognition of a "RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET" and a corresponding LEASE LIABILITY for SUBSTANTIALLY ALL leases — a MAJOR reform bringing J-GAAP's lease accounting CLOSE ALIGNMENT with IFRS 16, ending Japan's EXTENDED period of retaining an "old IAS 17"-style approach.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope and Effective Date</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">All lessees, effective from fiscal years beginning April 1, 2027</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies that are LESSEES (with some continued distinctions for LESSOR accounting), effective for FISCAL YEARS beginning ON OR AFTER APRIL 1, 2027 — giving companies a MULTI-YEAR transition period from the 2024 issuance date to PREPARE for the significant Balance Sheet impact this reform will have.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Redefining a Lease — Alignment With IFRS 16</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A contract conveying the right to control use of an identified asset</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">This Statement REDEFINES what constitutes a "LEASE" to ALIGN with IFRS 16's OWN definition — a contract that CONVEYS the right to CONTROL the use of an IDENTIFIED asset for a period of TIME in exchange for consideration — a genuinely NEW starting point for analysis, REPLACING the OLDER, more form-based lease identification criteria under the PREVIOUS standard.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>The Single On-Balance-Sheet Lessee Model</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">No more off-balance-sheet operating leases</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">UNDER the NEW model, a LESSEE recognises a RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET and a LEASE LIABILITY for VIRTUALLY ALL leases — ELIMINATING the OLD "operating lease" category's off-balance-sheet treatment ENTIRELY (subject to the narrow exemptions in Section 7) — a SINGLE, UNIFIED lessee accounting model REPLACING the PREVIOUS dual finance/operating classification.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Initial Measurement of the Right-of-Use Asset and Lease Liability</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Present value of lease payments, plus adjustments</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The LEASE LIABILITY is initially measured at the PRESENT VALUE of remaining LEASE PAYMENTS, discounted using the RATE implicit in the lease (or, where not readily determinable, the lessee's INCREMENTAL borrowing rate). The RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET is initially measured at COST — GENERALLY the initial lease liability amount, PLUS any lease payments made AT OR BEFORE commencement, initial DIRECT costs, and estimated RESTORATION costs (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 18, Asset Retirement Obligations, poster).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Subsequent Measurement</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Depreciation of the asset, interest accretion on the liability</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET is DEPRECIATED (generally straight-line) over the SHORTER of the lease term or the asset's useful life. The LEASE LIABILITY is REDUCED as payments are made, with INTEREST expense accreting the liability over time — broadly PARALLELING how a FINANCE lease was already treated under the OLD standard, now EXTENDED to cover leases that would PREVIOUSLY have been classified as operating leases.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Exemptions — Short-Term and Low-Value Leases</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Narrow relief, broadly mirroring IFRS 16's own exceptions</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A lessee MAY elect NOT to apply the on-balance-sheet model to SHORT-TERM leases (generally 12 months or less, with NO purchase option) or leases of LOW-VALUE underlying assets — recognising lease payments as an EXPENSE on a STRAIGHT-LINE basis instead, broadly MIRRORING the SAME narrow exemptions available under IFRS 16.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>J-GAAP-Specific Simplifications</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Practical simplifications appropriate to J-GAAP's user base</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">While BROADLY aligned with IFRS 16's overall ARCHITECTURE, ASBJ Statement No. 34 incorporates SEVERAL practical SIMPLIFICATIONS appropriate to Japan's SPECIFIC preparer base — reflecting the ASBJ's GENERAL preference for PROPORTIONATE, PRACTICAL guidance RATHER than a word-for-word replication of the international standard's EVERY provision.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Initial Recognition of a Lease</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Recognising the right-of-use asset and lease liability</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A 5-year office lease</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company enters a 5-year office lease with annual payments of ¥20,000,000, discounted using an incremental borrowing rate of 3%, giving a present value of lease payments of ¥91,600,000 (approximately).</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET and a LEASE LIABILITY of approximately <strong>¥91,600,000</strong> EACH at commencement — a MATERIAL new Balance Sheet recognition that would NOT have occurred under the OLD operating lease treatment (which would have simply expensed ¥20,000,000 per year straight-line, off-balance-sheet).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Applying the Short-Term Lease Exemption</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Retaining off-balance-sheet treatment for a genuinely short lease</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A 6-month equipment rental</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company rents specialised equipment for a 6-month project, with no purchase option or expectation of renewal, at ¥2,000,000 per month.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company ELECTS the SHORT-TERM lease exemption, recognising ¥2,000,000 of RENTAL EXPENSE each month on a straight-line basis — WITHOUT recognising a right-of-use asset or lease liability, given the lease's genuinely SHORT (12 months or less) term.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 34 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Right-of-use assets and lease liabilities recognised, by class of underlying asset</span>
          <span>Maturity analysis of lease liabilities</span>
          <span>Information about short-term/low-value lease exemptions elected</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Determining the lease term, including renewal/termination options reasonably certain to be exercised</span>
              <span>Whether a contract meets the redefined "lease" criteria at all</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Incremental borrowing rate where the rate implicit in the lease is not readily determinable</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13">
      <span class="num">13</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS 16</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Feature</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 34)</span>
            <span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IFRS 16)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Lessee model</span>
            <span>Single on-balance-sheet model</span>
            <span>Single on-balance-sheet model — converged</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12">
            <span>Short-term/low-value exemptions</span>
            <span>Available</span>
            <span>Available — converged</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A GENUINELY MAJOR convergence achievement — ending Japan's DECADES-LONG retention of an "old IAS 17"-style dual classification model, though on a DELAYED implementation timeline (effective 2027) relative to IFRS 16's OWN earlier effective date internationally.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14">
      <span class="num">14</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every lease event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Lease commencement</span>
            <span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span>
            <span>Right-of-use asset and lease liability recognised</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Depreciation and interest</span>
            <span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span>
            <span>Depreciation on the asset, interest accretion on the liability</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15">
      <span class="num">15</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 13</span>
            <span>The superseded old dual-classification lease standard</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 18</span>
            <span>Asset Retirement Obligations — relevant for lease-related restoration cost estimates</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s16">
      <span class="num">16</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Right-of-use asset</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The asset recognised by a lessee representing its right to use a leased asset over the lease term.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Incremental borrowing rate</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The rate a lessee would have to pay to borrow funds to obtain an asset of similar value, used to discount lease payments when the rate implicit in the lease is not readily determinable.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
